            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"Your diagram accurately shows unchanged demand and a leftward shift of wheat supply from S1 to S2, with clearly identified initial and new equilibria.\",\"The written explanation gives a complete causal chain: drought lowers harvests, supply falls at each price, a shortage occurs at P1, and price rises while quantity traded falls.\",\"Terminology and labels are precise and consistently match the wheat-market context.\"],\"improvements\":[],\"mistakes\":[],\"examinerComment\":\"Estimated practice result: 4/4. The diagram and explanation are fully consistent. You clearly connect reduced harvests to a contraction of supply, excess demand at the original equilibrium price, and the resulting higher equilibrium price and lower equilibrium quantity.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise distinguishing a shift in supply from a movement along a supply curve, then apply the same diagram logic to demand increases and decreases.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_2_c_to_f_diagram_and_explanation\",\"paper\":\"paper_2\",\"questionPart\":\"unknown\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\",\"application\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_2\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"2.3\",\"topicLabel\":\"Competitive market equilibrium\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":true,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"submitted_and_assessed\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"diagram\",\"assessableEarned\":4,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Knowledge and terminology\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Uses accurate terminology including supply shift, shortage, equilibrium price, quantity demanded and quantity traded.\"},{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Explains the full adjustment process from reduced harvests and lower supply to shortage, rising price and lower equilibrium quantity.\"},{\"label\":\"Application to context\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Applies the analysis directly to the drought and wheat market, with unchanged demand.\"},{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Readable wheat-market diagram has correctly labelled axes, unchanged D, S1 shifting left/up to S2, two equilibria, and higher P2 with lower Q2.\"}],\"bandRationale\":null,\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":{\"diagram\":2,\"explanation\":2,\"diagramReason\":\"The submitted diagram correctly shows the wheat price and quantity axes, unchanged D, S2 left/up of S1, and two demand–supply equilibria. Its labels and guide lines establish P2 above P1 and Q2 left of Q1.\",\"explanationReason\":\"The explanation accurately links the drought to less wheat supplied at each price, a shortage at P1, price competition, and the new equilibrium with higher price and lower quantity traded.\",\"incompatibleMechanisms\":false,\"mismatchEvidence\":\"\",\"labelingDeficiency\":false,\"labelingEvidence\":\"\",\"rootErrors\":[]}}"
          }
